<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tetrapolitan Confession</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1530">1530</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Tetrapolitan Confession was a Protestant statement of faith presented at the Diet of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/augsburg">Augsburg</a> in 1530 by four south German imperial cities: Strasbourg, Constance, Memmingen and Lindau. Drafted mainly by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/martin-bucer">Martin Bucer</a> and Wolfgang Capito, it stood between Lutheran and Zwinglian views, especially on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eucharist">Lord's Supper</a>. The cities later moved closer to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lutheranism">Lutheranism</a>.</p></div>
